# The table editor, the scores as a grid (tests/t1/pinball3d_editor_rules.sh). Written by guided.py.
# The rules themselves selected, the grid takes the place of the top view. The bumpers give 750 points for a hit
# instead of 500: the number of the rule that scores there. The lanes have three rules for a ball that rolls over
# them; the cell is the one without a condition.
4 key g meta
5 text rules
6 key Enter
8 key k meta
9 text pops
11 key Tab
12 text 750
13 key Enter
15 key k meta
16 text lanes
18 key Tab
19 text 350
20 key Enter
# A gate that scored nothing gets a rule; a flipper whose rule shifts the lane lights now scores too, in that rule.
23 key k meta
24 text laneGate
26 key Tab
27 text 150
28 key Enter
30 key k meta
31 text left
33 key Tab
34 text 25
35 key Enter
# The bank of drop targets has two cells, hit and down: the second is its 2000 points. 0 empties a cell: the standup
# targets keep their bonus and score nothing, the rule of the slingshots, which only scored, goes.
37 key k meta
38 text bank
40 key Tab
41 key Tab
42 text 2500
43 key Enter
45 key k meta
46 text stand
48 key Tab
49 text 0
50 key Enter
52 key k meta
